Current Version can be found [[Dark Ponman|here]].
Dark Ponman was added in '''Beta 39.0''' as a 4G 4/3 with a Magic effect that would return a [[Ponman]] from your dustpile back to your hand. '''Beta 45.0''' buffed that by returning 2 Ponmen.

'''Beta 46.0''' added [[Chessboard]] and the [[:Category:Piece|Piece]] Tribe with 5 members, this being one of them. As a result, it was entirely reworked. In stats, it only gain -1 ATK. In effect, like the others, it uses the same "played left or right" type of effect already used by [[Mister Society|Mr. Society]]. In this case, instead of giving positive stats/effects to itself or an ally Piece, it gives negative ones to an enemy monster of your choice: Paralyze if played left, Silence if played right. '''Beta 49.0''' turned it (and [[Final Froggit]]) from a [[:Category:Common|Common]] to a [[:Category:Rare|Rare]] in order to not make it (and [[:Category:Frog|Frogs]]) as effective in a deck that included [[Starwalker Bird]] and the likes.

'''Beta 49.1''' reworked it again (while giving its old design to [[Parsnik]]). Gaining +1 in both HP and Cost, as well as a Synergy effect that is identical to its Magic (making it effectively trigger its Magic twice if the conditions are right), its new effect makes it deal 2 DMG to a random enemy monster if played left, or draw a card if played right. During the next big Piece change of '''Beta 54.0''', Dark Ponman was returned to a 3 HP Common, but its cost also dropped to 3G, lost its Synergy and was given another new Magic. If played left, the next Piece in your deck would gain +1/+1. If played right, you would draw a Piece. If you have a [[Chessboard]] on the board, both effects will trigger, effectively drawing a Piece with +1/+1.
